## Translation-generated algebras and weak additivity

The algebra $`\mathfrak{A}_{\mathbf{B}}` is the C\*-subalgebra of $`\mathfrak{U}` generated by all
translates of the local algebra of $`\mathbf{B}`
([def:translation-generated-algebra](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#def:translation-generated-algebra)).
In Lean it is the topological closure of `StarAlgebra.adjoin` of the union of the ranges of the
embeddings $`\iota_{\mathbf{B} + x}`:

{docstring Physicslib4.AQFT.HaagKastler.HaagKastlerNet.translationGeneratedAlgebra}

Weak additivity
([def:weak-additivity](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#def:weak-additivity))
says it is all of $`\mathfrak{U}`, written as equality with `⊤` in the lattice of star subalgebras:

{docstring Physicslib4.AQFT.HaagKastler.HaagKastlerNet.IsWeaklyAdditive}

The von Neumann form
([def:weak-additivity-von-neumann](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#def:weak-additivity-von-neumann))
takes the commutant in the bounded operators on $`H` as Mathlib's `Set.centralizer`, as the local
von Neumann algebras do:

{docstring Physicslib4.AQFT.HaagKastler.HaagKastlerNet.IsWeaklyAdditiveVonNeumann}

The first implication between them
([lmm:weak-additivity-von-neumann](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#lmm:weak-additivity-von-neumann))
holds for every representation:

```lean (name := checkWAVN)
open Physicslib4 AQFT HaagKastler in
#check
  HaagKastlerNet.IsWeaklyAdditive.isWeaklyAdditiveVonNeumann
```

```leanOutput checkWAVN
Physicslib4.AQFT.HaagKastler.HaagKastlerNet.IsWeaklyAdditive.isWeaklyAdditiveVonNeumann.{u_1, u_2} {H : Type u_1}
  [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {N : HaagKastlerNet} (hN : N.IsWeaklyAdditive)
  (π : N.quasilocal.carrier →⋆ₐ[ℂ] H →L[ℂ] H) : N.IsWeaklyAdditiveVonNeumann π
```

## The theorem

The main theorem
([thrm:reeh-schlieder](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#thrm:reeh-schlieder))
has four groups of hypotheses. The covariant setting is `π`, `Ω`, `U` and `hU`, the implementation
condition $`U(x)\pi(a)\Omega = \pi(\beta_x a)\Omega`. Positive energy is `hpos`: for every $`n` in
the open forward cone, `IsPositiveEnergy fun t => U (t • n)`. The geometry is `hB₁B`: eventually
in the neighbourhood filter of $`0`, that is, for every $`x` in some neighbourhood of $`0`,
$`\mathbf{B}_1 + x \subseteq \mathbf{B}`. The conclusion is pointwise: for every
$`A \in \mathfrak{A}_{\mathbf{B}_1}`, $`\pi(A)\Omega` lies in the closure of the orbit of
$`\Omega` under the local algebra of $`\mathbf{B}`.

```lean (name := checkRS)
open Physicslib4 AQFT HaagKastler in
#check reeh_schlieder
```

```leanOutput checkRS
Physicslib4.AQFT.HaagKastler.reeh_schlieder.{u_1, u_2} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]
  [CompleteSpace H] {N : HaagKastlerNet} (π : N.quasilocal.carrier →⋆ₐ[ℂ] H →L[ℂ] H) (Ω : H)
  (U : StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier → H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H)
  (hU :
    ∀ (x : StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier) (a : N.quasilocal.carrier),
      (U x) ((π a) Ω) = (π ((N.action (translationSub x)) a)) Ω)
  (hpos : ∀ n ∈ minkowskiForwardCone 0, IsPositiveEnergy fun t => U (t • n))
  {B₁ B : Set StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier} (hB₁ : IsAlexandrovBasisSet B₁) (hB : IsAlexandrovBasisSet B)
  (hB₁B : ∀ᶠ (x : StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier) in nhds 0, translationSub x • B₁ ⊆ B) (A : N.quasilocal.carrier) :
  A ∈ N.translationGeneratedAlgebra hB₁ → (π A) Ω ∈ closure (Set.range fun b => (π ((N.quasilocal.ι hB) b)) Ω)
```

## The cyclicity corollaries

The first corollary
([crllr:reeh-schlieder-cyclic](https://physicslib.github.io/physicslib4/blueprint/chptr-haag-kastler-axioms-blueprint.html#crllr:reeh-schlieder-cyclic))
assumes `hcyc`, cyclicity of $`\Omega` for $`\pi(\mathfrak{A}_{\mathbf{B}'})` for every nonempty
diamond $`\mathbf{B}'`. Given a nonempty diamond $`\mathbf{B}`, it picks a smaller nonempty
diamond $`\mathbf{B}_1` all of whose small translates stay in $`\mathbf{B}`, and applies the main
theorem. The conclusion uses `HaagKastlerNet.localOperators`, the set of operators
$`\pi(\iota_{\mathbf{B}}(b))`.

```lean (name := checkRSCyclic)
open Physicslib4 AQFT HaagKastler in
#check reeh_schlieder_cyclic
```

```leanOutput checkRSCyclic
Physicslib4.AQFT.HaagKastler.reeh_schlieder_cyclic.{u_1, u_2} {H : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup H]
  [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H] {N : HaagKastlerNet} (π : N.quasilocal.carrier →⋆ₐ[ℂ] H →L[ℂ] H) (Ω : H)
  (U : StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier → H ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] H)
  (hU :
    ∀ (x : StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier) (a : N.quasilocal.carrier),
      (U x) ((π a) Ω) = (π ((N.action (translationSub x)) a)) Ω)
  (hpos : ∀ n ∈ minkowskiForwardCone 0, IsPositiveEnergy fun t => U (t • n))
  (hcyc :
    ∀ ⦃B' : Set StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier⦄ (hB' : IsAlexandrovBasisSet B'),
      B'.Nonempty → Dense (Set.range fun a => (π ↑a) Ω))
  {B : Set StandardMinkowskiSpacetime.Carrier} (hB : IsAlexandrovBasisSet B) (hne : B.Nonempty) :
  Dense ((fun T => T Ω) '' N.localOperators π hB)
```

